  "title": "I-CARE: International Cardiac Arrest REsearch consortium EEG Database (BIDS)",
  "description": "The I-CARE database contains continuous EEG and, where available, ECG recordings with baseline clinical information from comatose adults after cardiac arrest. Data were assembled by seven academic hospitals in the United States, the Netherlands and Belgium for neurological prognostication. This BIDS conversion of PhysioNet release 2.1 covers 607 patients and 36,123 hourly recordings, with outcomes given as dichotomised Cerebral Performance Category.",
  "methods_description": "Continuous EEG was recorded using standard 10-20 electrodes (19-21 channels), with ECG and reference channels where present. Sampling rates varied by site (200-2048 Hz). Monitoring began within hours of return of spontaneous circulation and continued for hours to days. WFDB records were losslessly converted to EDF per hourly segment, with units inferred as microvolts.",
